==Enemy==
Compared to [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]], Director Kurosawah has a faster attack rate, much higher damage and longer range. His huge range of 700 makes it difficult for most [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark units]] like [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Cooldown Cat]] and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] to get an attack off.

Due to strength magnifications, Kurosawah is generally more of a glass cannon than Nyandam, who tends to have higher health than Kurosawahs encountered around the same point. In 1-crown stages, Kurosawah's health peaks at 960k, whereas Nyandam's can reach over 3.3 million.

Even at lower strength magnifications, Kurosawah can often destroy an entire stack of cats in a single hit, sometimes even your [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] and [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rares]]. This makes him a formidable threat if you aren't able to knock him back in time or push too far into his range, leaving you to rebuild the stack you just created.

==Strategy==
Director Kurosawah is similar to the original Nyandam with his long attack animation, but his massive range invalidates almost all other units because he'll just delete them in one hit. His long attack animation can be exploited by any effect that causes enemies to be displaced, such as knockback, the default [[Cat Cannon]], [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Recruit]]. Bombercat can essentially stun-lock him, but as with other Dark backliners, it can be difficult to find an opening.

Rushers and strong melee units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]], [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], and [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Sanada Yukimura]] are particularly effective against Kurosawah if there are no enemies in the way. They can easily reach and deal fairly significant damage to him, but this can be inconsistent, as he often appears backing frontline melee threats. [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] don't have to wander into his range in order to hit him provided there are frontline enemies to use as stepping stones, though for consistency their Wave level needs to be at or exceed 3.

